{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>All the firstborn.</b> After he set forth the kinds of kindness in produce — that is, the poor man's tithe — and in money — that is, the release of debts and charity — and in other possessions — that is, the freeing of the Hebrew slave — he now sets forth commandments through which one gives thanks to El, exalted be He. These are: the giving of firstlings, which is fitting for owners of livestock, to give thanks that the livestock come to us from His hand; and the Festival of Matzot, to give thanks for the redemption through the Pesach sacrifice and matzot, and for the spring season through the waving of the omer; and the Festival of Weeks, to give thanks for the weeks of harvest statutes that He kept for us; and the Festival of Ingathering, to give thanks for the ingathering. And in each of them one brings a gift to the Master, as it says: וְלֹא יֵרָאֶה אֶת פְּנֵי ה׳ רֵיקָם (Deuteronomy 16:16). Therefore Scripture does not mention for them in which month or on what day of the month they fall, but rather mentions the spring, the weeks, and the ingathering."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:31.690107608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}